      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9977ee91-683e-562c-9427-8ecba6a0432b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Desaga, Michael Faraday, Robert Wilhelm Bunsen, Nicolae Teclu\n- Places: University of Heidelberg\n- Products: Bunsen burner, Teclu burner, laboratory burner\n- Topics: instrument making, electromagnetism, electrochemistry\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Faraday was an English scientist who lived from 22 September 1791 to 25 August 1867 and contributed to electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\n- In 1855, Peter Desaga perfected an earlier laboratory burner design by Michael Faraday into the Bunsen burner.\n- Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\n- Robert Wilhelm Bunsen and his laboratory assistant Peter Desaga developed the Bunsen burner as an improvement on laboratory burners then in use.\n- The Teclu burner is a laboratory gas burner that is a variant of the Bunsen burner and is named after the Romanian chemist Nicolae Teclu.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
